# 🌐 Gazelle Web Application

[![Streamlit App](https://static.streamlit.io/badges/streamlit_badge_black_white.svg)](https://gazelle.streamlit.app/)
[![Dataset](https://img.shields.io/badge/Kaggle-Dataset-blue?logo=kaggle)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/jeffreybraun/running-log-insight)
[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.9+-green?logo=python)](https://www.python.org/)

Gazelle is an interactive web application designed to analyze running logs and predict performance metrics using fine-tuned machine learning models.

---

## 🔗 Quick Links

- **Live Demo:** [gazelle.streamlit.app](https://gazelle.streamlit.app/)
- **Data Source:** [Kaggle – Running Log Insight](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/jeffreybraun/running-log-insight)

---

## 📂 Repository Structure

The core codebase is organized into modular scripts for model training, visualization, and application deployment:

| File | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **`ForestFineTune.py`** | Hyperparameter fine-tuning pipeline for the Random Forest model. |
| **`Plotter.py`** | Visualizes train vs. test set error curves across decision tree depths to identify optimal hyperparameter thresholds. |
| **`Predictor.py`** | Contains the core prediction logic and feature engineering pipelines. |
| **`WebApp.py`** | Main entry point combining the prediction backend with the interactive Streamlit UI. |

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

Ensure you have Python installed along with the required dependencies:

```bash
pip install streamlit scikit-learn pandas numpy matplotlib
